skills.card:
expectedValue — Work out the expected value of a set of outcomes and their probabilities.
  needs: outcomes: array
  e.g. "expected value of a coin flip for 100 or minus 50" → {"outcomes":[{"value":100,"probability":0.5},{"value":-50,"probability":0.5}]}

whatPercent — Work out what share one number is of another, as a percentage — what proportion 18 is of 24, or a score out of a maximum.
  needs: part: number, whole: number
  e.g. "36 out of 240 as a percentage" → {"part":36,"whole":240}

scaleRecipe — Multiply every ingredient amount in a recipe by a factor, rounded to sensible kitchen fractions.
  needs: ingredients: array, factor: number
  e.g. "double this recipe: 2 cups flour, 1 egg, 3/4 tsp salt" → {"ingredients":["2 cups flour","1 egg","3/4 tsp salt"],"factor":2}

convertLength — Convert a distance or length — millimetres, centimetres, metres, kilometres, inches, feet, yards, miles.
  needs: amount: number, from: string, to: string
  e.g. "how many km is 26.2 miles" → {"amount":26.2,"from":"miles","to":"km"}

convertTime — Convert a length of time between units — how long 210 minutes runs to in hours.
  needs: amount: number, from: string, to: string
  e.g. "how many hours is 5400 seconds" → {"amount":5400,"from":"s","to":"h"}

rollDice — Roll dice in standard notation like 2d6+3, from a seed so the same roll can be repeated.
  needs: notation: string, seed: integer
  e.g. "roll 2d6 with seed 7" → {"notation":"2d6","seed":7}

generatePassphrase — Generate a memorable passphrase from random words.
  optional: words: integer, separator: string, capitalise: boolean, number: boolean
  e.g. "generate a passphrase" → {}

countdownTo — Count how long until a date, or how long since one, from today. Takes the one date.
  needs: to: string
  e.g. "how many days till my sister's wedding on nov 14" → {"to":"2026-11-14"}

gradeNeeded — Work out what score the remaining work needs to reach a target grade.
  needs: current: number, completed: number, target: number
  e.g. "what do I need on the final to get 80 percent" → {"current":78,"completed":70,"target":80}

bmiCalculate — Work out body mass index from a height and weight — the formula only.
  needs: weightKg: number, heightCm: number
  e.g. "bmi for 70kg and 175cm" → {"weightKg":70,"heightCm":175}
